{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MxJtctD8UdS2Kp1xGW8oc6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Curriculum Decision Log\n2\t\n3\t*Append-only record of editorial decisions John has made on the curriculum. Each entry: date, decision, who recommended, what was selected, why. Do not rewrite history; new decisions go at the top, retired decisions get a strikethrough with a \"retired YYYY-MM-DD\" line.*\n4\t\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t## 2026-05-06 PM â€” Five stub dispositions resolved (autonomous greenlit)\n8\t\n9\tFive stubs left over from prior phases were resolved in a single autonomous pass following Phase 8.4 (Spanish track scaffolding) and the 2026-05-04 PM Phase 4 #4 elementary-stub decision. Group A (modern-language stubs superseded by the new Spanish track) and Group B (elementary stubs kept as real gaps) were both addressed.\n10\t\n11\t### Decision â€” Group A: Modern-language stubs superseded by Phase 8.4 Spanish track\n12\t\n13\t| Course | Disposition | Rationale |\n14\t|---|---|---|\n15\t| `middle/grade-7/Latin-6-or-Modern-Language-1/` | **Reframed** as Latin-track-only (Track field + README rewritten) | Directory contains a fully-built Latin 6 / Henle First Year Part B course, not a stub; the \"or-Modern-Language-1\" suffix in the folder name was a legacy placeholder. With Phase 8.4 installing the Spanish complete track at its own G7 slot (`Spanish-2-Intermediate/`), Latin and Spanish are now parallel courses, not an either-or. Folder rename queued for a supervised cleanup pass (sandbox cannot rename). |\n16\t| `middle/grade-8/Modern-Language-2/` | **Retired** (REPLACED-BY redirect to `Spanish-3-Pre-Conversational/`) | Generic stub fully superseded by the populated `Spanish-3-Pre-Conversational` course built in Phase 8.4 (covers subjunctive introduction, future and conditional, *por*/*para*, first literary readings â€” exactly the M-L-2 scope). SYLLABUS + README rewritten as redirect notices. Directory preserved (sandbox cannot delete); deletion queued for a supervised pass. |\n17\t\n18\t**Why.** Phase 8.4's decision (DECISION-LOG 2026-05-04 PM) to install Spanish as the K-12 modern-language complete track makes the generic \"Modern-Language-N\" placeholders structurally redundant â€” Spanish *is* the modern language. The Group A retirements close the loop on Phase 8.4's scope.\n19\t\n20\t**Downstream.** Two STUB entries removed from the canonical stub-grep (`grep -rln \"^> \\*\\*STUB\\.\\*\\*\" --include=\"SYLLABUS.md\"` per ORCHESTRATOR-STATE rule Â§8). Folder cleanup (rename + delete) queued for a future supervised session.\n21\t\n22\t### Decision â€” Group B: Three elementary stubs built as stub-with-spec\n23\t\n24\t| Course | Disposition | Rationale |\n25\t|---|---|---|\n26\t| `elementary/grade-4/Grammar-Diagramming/` | **Stub-with-spec built** (~1,300 words) | DECISION-LOG 2026-05-04 PM (Phase 4 #4) kept as real gap. Spine: Mary Daly *Diagramming the Sentences of the Catechism of the Catholic Church* (Reed-Kellogg tradition primary); Reed & Kellogg *Graded Lessons in English* 1875 (public domain alternate). 6 units / 120 lessons / 60 hours. Co-runs in parallel with `K4-WRITING-WISE-BAUER-WWE`. Synthesis instrument: visual-diff machine grading on diagram correctness. |\n27\t| `elementary/grade-4/Writing-Wise-Bauer-WWE/` | **Stub-with-spec built** (~1,400 words) | DECISION-LOG 2026-05-04 PM kept as real gap. Spine: Susan Wise Bauer *The Complete Writer: Writing With Ease, Level 4* (commercial primary); McGuffey *Fourth Eclectic Reader* (1879, public domain alternate). 8 units / 140 lessons / 70 hours. Source-passage roster: Beatrix Potter / E. B. White / C. S. Lewis / Wilder / Stevenson / Story-of-the-World. Hand-off bridges into the populated `K5-WRITING-WISE-BAUER-WWS-1` at G5. |\n28\t| `elementary/grade-5/Grammar-Complete/` | **Stub-with-spec built** (~1,700 words) | DECISION-LOG 2026-05-04 PM kept as real gap. Spine: Rod & Staff *English 5: Following the Plan* (Mennonite-classical primary); Loyola *Voyages in English 5* (Catholic-classical alternate); McGuffey *Fifth Eclectic Reader* + Warriner's *First Course* (open-license alternate). 8 units / 140 lessons / 94 hours. Capstone: parsing-and-diagramming portfolio defended orally. Hand-off bridges into M6 Latin (comparative grammar) + M6 Spanish (morphological grammar) + M6 Writing-With-Skill-2. |\n29\t\n30\t**Why.** All three are real curricular gaps per the prior decision; building stub-with-spec turns each from \"scaffold awaiting decision\" into \"specification ready for build\" without front-running the supervised Wave-2-elementary unit-body pass. Each SYLLABUS is intentionally written as a *brief for the future build* â€” spine selected, unit list complete, assessment shape fixed â€” so the build can proceed without re-deciding scope.\n31\t\n32\t**Downstream.** Three STUB entries replaced by populated SYLLABUSes in the canonical stub-grep. Wave-2-elementary build (Phase 5 round 2 or later â€” currently not on the dispatcher plan per ORCHESTRATOR-STATE 2026-05-04) is the natural unit-body home; recommendation: add Wave-2-elementary to the next Phase 5 round. SKILL-INDEX rebuild can wait until that pass.\n33\t\n34\t### Constraints honored on both groups\n35\t\n36\t- `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\` only; no OneDrive paths touched.\n37\t- No git operations.\n38\t- No deletion attempts after the first sandbox-blocked attempt; Group A retirement handled via REPLACED-BY content overwrites (precedent: Phase 8.5 Char-6, ORCHESTRATOR-STATE 2026-05-06).\n39\t- All five dispositions are reversible.\n40\t\n41\t### Session log\n42\t\n43\t`Curriculum/SESSION-LOG-2026-05-06-Stub-Dispositions.md` â€” five-row table + per-file change list + advisory flags.\n44\t\n45\t---\n46\t\n47\t## 2026-05-04 PM â€” Phase 4 quarantined decisions resolved\n48\t\n49\tThree Phase 4 sub-decisions settled in the interactive walkthrough following the autonomous overnight run.\n50\t\n51\t### Decision â€” Modern-language strategic call (Phase 4 #3)\n52\t\n53\t**Selected: Latin + Spanish.**\n54\t\n55\tLatin remains baked into the curriculum spine (Latin-3-Cicero G9 etc.). Spanish is added as the modern-language complete track.\n56\t\n57\t**Why.** Spanish has the largest free OER curriculum corpus available, the highest practical-fluency value for an American homeschool student, and matches what Hillsdale K-12 reference schools do. The single-modern-language choice (vs Spanish + French) keeps Phase 7b/8.4 editorial scope manageable; a third modern language can be added in a Phase 9 enhancement.\n58\t\n59\t**Downstream.** Phase 8.4 (Modern Language complete track) is greenlit-pending-Phase-6. The track will build Spanish across G6-G12 (~6 course slots).\n60\t\n61\t### Decision â€” American-History-Hillsdale-11 (Phase 4 #2)\n62\t\n63\t**Selected: Defer until Phase 6 transcripts are in.**\n64\t\n65\tThe course is not built; not deleted; queued for build after Phase 6 (next 10 Hillsdale Online courses) lands.\n66\t\n67\t**Why.** Phase 3 (completed 2026-05-04) gave the curriculum 22 lectures of candidate spine material â€” *American Heritage* (12) and *The Great American Story* (10). Phase 6 will add the remainder of the relevant Hillsdale Online stack. Building the course before Phase 6 means rebuilding it once the additional sources land. Defer-then-build is cheaper than build-now-then-redo.\n68\t\n69\t**Downstream.** When Phase 6 completes, this course enters the Phase 7b build queue alongside the Health/PE thread and the Character 9-12 sequence.\n70\t\n71\t### Decision â€” Four elementary stubs (Phase 4 #4)\n72\t\n73\tReviewed each:\n74\t\n75\t| Course | Disposition | Rationale |\n76\t|---|---|---|\n77\t| `elementary/grade-4/Grammar-Diagramming/` | **Keep as real gap** | Diagramming is its own discipline, complements the existing G3 Grammar-Parts-of-Speech course. Queue for a future Wave-2-elementary build pass. |\n78\t| `elementary/grade-4/Writing-Wise-Bauer-WWE/` | **Keep as real gap** | WWE (Writing With Ease) is the elementary precursor to the populated G5 Writing-Wise-Bauer-WWS-1. Real gap; build later. |\n79\t| `elementary/grade-5/Grammar-Complete/` | **Keep as real gap** | Capstone consolidating G3 + G4 grammar. Real gap; build later. |\n80\t| `elementary/grade-5/Writing-Wise-Bauer-WWS-1/` | **Reclassify â€” NOT a stub** | On inspection, this syllabus is fully populated (course aim, spine text, 6 units, assessment weights). It was misclassified in the FLAG list. Remove from stub list. |\n81\t\n82\t**Why.** Three are real curricular gaps that should be filled in a future supervised pass; one was an inspection error. None is a duplicate worth deleting.\n83\t\n84\t**Downstream.** STUB count drops by one (the misclassified WWS-1 removes from the list). The three remaining stubs queue for Wave-2-elementary, which is not in the current Phase 5 dispatcher plan but should be added when Phase 5 humanities round 2 sequencing is set.\n85\t\n86\t---\n87\t\n88\t*Authored 2026-05-04 PM by Cowork (Claude Opus 4.7) during the interactive walkthrough of the autonomous overnight run. Standing rules: append-only; new decisions at top; retired decisions strikethrough with retire date.*\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b7e5f35-a95a-44e2-8d31-68bd9378bb04","uuid":"dd6cc8cc-66a8-4536-8870-2ddcec33a4cc","timestamp":"2026-06-23T00:55:20.722Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\Curriculum\\DECISION-LOG.md","content":"# Curriculum Decision Log\n\n*Append-only record of editorial decisions John has made on the curriculum. Each entry: date, decision, who recommended, what was selected, why. Do not rewrite history; new decisions go at the top, retired decisions get a strikethrough with a \"retired YYYY-MM-DD\" line.*\n\n---\n\n## 2026-05-06 PM â€” Five stub dispositions resolved (autonomous greenlit)\n\nFive stubs left over from prior phases were resolved in a single autonomous pass following Phase 8.4 (Spanish track scaffolding) and the 2026-05-04 PM Phase 4 #4 elementary-stub decision. Group A (modern-language stubs superseded by the new Spanish track) and Group B (elementary stubs kept as real gaps) were both addressed.\n\n### Decision â€” Group A: Modern-language stubs superseded by Phase 8.4 Spanish track\n\n| Course | Disposition | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| `middle/grade-7/Latin-6-or-Modern-Language-1/` | **Reframed** as Latin-track-only (Track field + README rewritten) | Directory contains a fully-built Latin 6 / Henle First Year Part B course, not a stub; the \"or-Modern-Language-1\" suffix in the folder name was a legacy placeholder. With Phase 8.4 installing the Spanish complete track at its own G7 slot (`Spanish-2-Intermediate/`), Latin and Spanish are now parallel courses, not an either-or. Folder rename queued for a supervised cleanup pass (sandbox cannot rename). |\n| `middle/grade-8/Modern-Language-2/` | **Retired** (REPLACED-BY redirect to `Spanish-3-Pre-Conversational/`) | Generic stub fully superseded by the populated `Spanish-3-Pre-Conversational` course built in Phase 8.4 (covers subjunctive introduction, future and conditional, *por*/*para*, first literary readings â€” exactly the M-L-2 scope). SYLLABUS + README rewritten as redirect notices. Directory preserved (sandbox cannot delete); deletion queued for a supervised pass. |\n\n**Why.** Phase 8.4's decision (DECISION-LOG 2026-05-04 PM) to install Spanish as the K-12 modern-language complete track makes the generic \"Modern-Language-N\" placeholders structurally redundant â€” Spanish *is* the modern language. The Group A retirements close the loop on Phase 8.4's scope.\n\n**Downstream.** Two STUB entries removed from the canonical stub-grep (`grep -rln \"^> \\*\\*STUB\\.\\*\\*\" --include=\"SYLLABUS.md\"` per ORCHESTRATOR-STATE rule Â§8). Folder cleanup (rename + delete) queued for a future supervised session.\n\n### Decision â€” Group B: Three elementary stubs built as stub-with-spec\n\n| Course | Disposition | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| `elementary/grade-4/Grammar-Diagramming/` | **Stub-with-spec built** (~1,300 words) | DECISION-LOG 2026-05-04 PM (Phase 4 #4) kept as real gap. Spine: Mary Daly *Diagramming the Sentences of the Catechism of the Catholic Church* (Reed-Kellogg tradition primary); Reed & Kellogg *Graded Lessons in English* 1875 (public domain alternate). 6 units / 120 lessons / 60 hours. Co-runs in parallel with `K4-WRITING-WISE-BAUER-WWE`. Synthesis instrument: visual-diff machine grading on diagram correctness. |\n| `elementary/grade-4/Writing-Wise-Bauer-WWE/` | **Stub-with-spec built** (~1,400 words) | DECISION-LOG 2026-05-04 PM kept as real gap. Spine: Susan Wise Bauer *The Complete Writer: Writing With Ease, Level 4* (commercial primary); McGuffey *Fourth Eclectic Reader* (1879, public domain alternate). 8 units / 140 lessons / 70 hours. Source-passage roster: Beatrix Potter / E. B. White / C. S. Lewis / Wilder / Stevenson / Story-of-the-World. Hand-off bridges into the populated `K5-WRITING-WISE-BAUER-WWS-1` at G5. |\n| `elementary/grade-5/Grammar-Complete/` | **Stub-with-spec built** (~1,700 words) | DECISION-LOG 2026-05-04 PM kept as real gap. Spine: Rod & Staff *English 5: Following the Plan* (Mennonite-classical primary); Loyola *Voyages in English 5* (Catholic-classical alternate); McGuffey *Fifth Eclectic Reader* + Warriner's *First Course* (open-license alternate). 8 units / 140 lessons / 94 hours. Capstone: parsing-and-diagramming portfolio defended orally. Hand-off bridges into M6 Latin (comparative grammar) + M6 Spanish (morphological grammar) + M6 Writing-With-Skill-2. |\n\n**Why.** All three are real curricular gaps per the prior decision; building stub-with-spec turns each from \"scaffold awaiting decision\" into \"specification ready for build\" without front-running the supervised Wave-2-elementary unit-body pass. Each SYLLABUS is intentionally written as a *brief for the future build* â€” spine selected, unit list complete, assessment shape fixed â€” so the build can proceed without re-deciding scope.\n\n**Downstream.** Three STUB entries replaced by populated SYLLABUSes in the canonical stub-grep. Wave-2-elementary build (Phase 5 round 2 or later â€” currently not on the dispatcher plan per ORCHESTRATOR-STATE 2026-05-04) is the natural unit-body home; recommendation: add Wave-2-elementary to the next Phase 5 round. SKILL-INDEX rebuild can wait until that pass.\n\n### Constraints honored on both groups\n\n- `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\` only; no OneDrive paths touched.\n- No git operations.\n- No deletion attempts after the first sandbox-blocked attempt; Group A retirement handled via REPLACED-BY content overwrites (precedent: Phase 8.5 Char-6, ORCHESTRATOR-STATE 2026-05-06).\n- All five dispositions are reversible.\n\n### Session log\n\n`Curriculum/SESSION-LOG-2026-05-06-Stub-Dispositions.md` â€” five-row table + per-file change list + advisory flags.\n\n---\n\n## 2026-05-04 PM â€” Phase 4 quarantined decisions resolved\n\nThree Phase 4 sub-decisions settled in the interactive walkthrough following the autonomous overnight run.\n\n### Decision â€” Modern-language strategic call (Phase 4 #3)\n\n**Selected: Latin + Spanish.**\n\nLatin remains baked into the curriculum spine (Latin-3-Cicero G9 etc.). Spanish is added as the modern-language complete track.\n\n**Why.** Spanish has the largest free OER curriculum corpus available, the highest practical-fluency value for an American homeschool student, and matches what Hillsdale K-12 reference schools do. The single-modern-language choice (vs Spanish + French) keeps Phase 7b/8.4 editorial scope manageable; a third modern language can be added in a Phase 9 enhancement.\n\n**Downstream.** Phase 8.4 (Modern Language complete track) is greenlit-pending-Phase-6. The track will build Spanish across G6-G12 (~6 course slots).\n\n### Decision â€” American-History-Hillsdale-11 (Phase 4 #2)\n\n**Selected: Defer until Phase 6 transcripts are in.**\n\nThe course is not built; not deleted; queued for build after Phase 6 (next 10 Hillsdale Online courses) lands.\n\n**Why.** Phase 3 (completed 2026-05-04) gave the curriculum 22 lectures of candidate spine material â€” *American Heritage* (12) and *The Great American Story* (10). Phase 6 will add the remainder of the relevant Hillsdale Online stack. Building the course before Phase 6 means rebuilding it once the additional sources land. Defer-then-build is cheaper than build-now-then-redo.\n\n**Downstream.** When Phase 6 completes, this course enters the Phase 7b build queue alongside the Health/PE thread and the Character 9-12 sequence.\n\n### Decision â€” Four elementary stubs (Phase 4 #4)\n\nReviewed each:\n\n| Course | Disposition | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| `elementary/grade-4/Grammar-Diagramming/` | **Keep as real gap** | Diagramming is its own discipline, complements the existing G3 Grammar-Parts-of-Speech course. Queue for a future Wave-2-elementary build pass. |\n| `elementary/grade-4/Writing-Wise-Bauer-WWE/` | **Keep as real gap** | WWE (Writing With Ease) is the elementary precursor to the populated G5 Writing-Wise-Bauer-WWS-1. Real gap; build later. |\n| `elementary/grade-5/Grammar-Complete/` | **Keep as real gap** | Capstone consolidating G3 + G4 grammar. Real gap; build later. |\n| `elementary/grade-5/Writing-Wise-Bauer-WWS-1/` | **Reclassify â€” NOT a stub** | On inspection, this syllabus is fully populated (course aim, spine text, 6 units, assessment weights). It was misclassified in the FLAG list. Remove from stub list. |\n\n**Why.** Three are real curricular gaps that should be filled in a future supervised pass; one was an inspection error. None is a duplicate worth deleting.\n\n**Downstream.** STUB count drops by one (the misclassified WWS-1 removes from the list). The three remaining stubs queue for Wave-2-elementary, which is not in the current Phase 5 dispatcher plan but should be added when Phase 5 humanities round 2 sequencing is set.\n\n---\n\n*Authored 2026-05-04 PM by Cowork (Claude Opus 4.7) during the interactive walkthrough of the autonomous overnight run. Standing rules: append-only; new decisions at top; retired decisions strikethrough with retire date.*\n","numLines":89,"startLine":1,"totalLines":89}}}
